# Every text file is stored LF in the repository; what lands in the working tree is the
# platform's business. The index is already uniformly LF, so this normalises nothing and
# changes no committed bytes — it stops the result depending on whether whoever cloned it
# happens to have core.autocrlf set.
* text=auto

# Windows-only scripts, and never run anywhere else. Some PowerShell hosts and editors
# still expect CRLF from a .ps1.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Read by tools rather than by a Windows shell, so keep them LF on every platform.
*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Marked in case one is ever committed despite .gitignore. Line-ending translation applied
# to a compiled assembly corrupts it, and it fails looking like a code bug rather than a
# mangled file.
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
*.zip binary
